    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "I fixed it in `ids.go`, but I could not run the tests because the permission prompt blocked `go test`.\n\nThe duplicates came from how `NewID` used the `next` file. It read the file, added one and wrote it back, with no lock. Two processes could read the same value at the same time and hand out the same id.\n\n`NewID` now returns a random id from `crypto/rand`, in UUID format (for example `3f2a9c1e-...`). It uses no shared file, so processes cannot race. The ids contain dashes, so a new id can never equal one of the old numeric ids. The `dir` parameter stays so that callers do not break, but the function no longer uses it.\n\nThis change has a limit. The uniqueness is random, with 122 random bits, so a repeat is possible in theory but not in practice. If you need a strict guarantee, each id must claim a marker file in `dir`, with one file per id.\n\nI added `ids_test.go`, which calls `NewID` 2000 times at once and checks for duplicates and bad characters.\n\n**TLDR**\nThe cause was an unlocked read and write of the `next` file. `NewID` now returns random UUID-form ids, and old numeric ids cannot collide with them.\nRun `go test ./...`, because I could not.",
